{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And you shall remember HaShem.</b> For from Him alone will come to you all good, for He it is who gives you the strength to make wealth — that is to say, He delivered into your hand the power of the constellations that He created to produce effects below, and He gave you dominion over them, and the constellations have no rule or dominion over you; and as the Rabbis, blessed be their memory, said: 'Israel has no constellation.' And this is what is said: 'that He may establish His covenant which He swore to your fathers' — for so He promised Abraham that all his seed would be above the constellations, and this is what the Rabbis, blessed be their memory, expounded on (Genesis 15:5) — ויוצא אותו החוצה ויאמר הבט נא השמימה — 'the expression הבט is only from above downward,' teaching that He raised him above the constellations, and said to him: כה יהיה זרעך." "<b>And according to</b> this, the subject of the parashah will be speaking of all Israel collectively, even though the language comes in singular form, for such is the way of Scripture; and so the parashah began with a mixture of singular and plural — כל המצוה אשר אנכי מצוך היום תשמרון לעשות. And if you say that it speaks of each individual of Israel, whether for the moment or for generations to come, and therefore the language comes in singular form, then the meaning of the verse will be: ואמרת בלבבך — that wealth is decreed from heaven for every single individual of Israel — for when they said 'Israel has no constellation,' they said it concerning the collective, but for each individual there is a constellation; and so they said: 'Children, life, and sustenance are not dependent on merit but on constellation' — the strength of the constellation of the wheel — ועוצם ידי למטה שאני נושא ונותן ומתעסק — the strength of my hand below, as I engage in trade and business — 'made me this wealth,' for through the combination of these two the wealth comes — do not imagine in your soul to say thus, but rather: וזכרת את ה' אלהיך כי הוא הנותן לך כח לעשות חיל — for that supernal strength that you have, He gave it to you, and with it you make wealth below; for without His strength, may He be exalted, there would be no power in the constellation at all, for He is supreme over all the powers, every one. And this is what Solomon, peace be upon him, said (Proverbs 22:2): עשיר ורש נפגשו עושה כלם ה' — he explains to you that wealth and poverty are an encounter and a meeting, occurring through the revolution of the wheel, and the wealth of the rich is not due to his wisdom and the strength of his hand, nor is the poverty of the poor due to a lack of his wisdom. And lest you say: if so, that wealth and poverty are an encounter and a meeting, then all is the decree of the supernal forces, and there is no decree of the Name at all, neither in the wealth of the rich nor in the poverty of the poor — if so, the matter is surrendered to the forces and to chance — therefore he said עושה כלם ה', to clarify that all is by the decree of the Supreme One upon them; through Him come wealth and poverty, evil and good."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:08.254905009Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}